1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,900
In this video, we're going to talk about

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,200
blood pressure and its two numbers.

3
00:00:07,944 --> 00:00:09,969
By the end, you'll know what blood

4
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:12,094
pressure measures, what systolic and

5
00:00:12,094 --> 00:00:14,569
diastolic mean, when a reading counts as

6
00:00:14,569 --> 00:00:16,832
high, and how to keep it healthy.

7
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:22,442
Most people with high blood pressure feel

8
00:00:22,442 --> 00:00:25,330
perfectly well, with no warning signs at

9
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:29,746
all. Yet inside, the pressure can stay

10
00:00:29,746 --> 00:00:32,789
high for years. The World Health

11
00:00:32,789 --> 00:00:35,713
Organization estimates that 46 percent of

12
00:00:35,713 --> 00:00:37,026
them don't know it.

13
00:00:38,259 --> 00:00:39,546
So how would you know?

14
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:44,546
So what is blood pressure?

15
00:00:45,729 --> 00:00:47,829
It is the force of blood pushing against

16
00:00:47,829 --> 00:00:49,454
the walls of your arteries.

17
00:00:50,665 --> 00:00:52,290
Let's look inside one!

18
00:00:53,489 --> 00:00:56,289
With every heartbeat, blood surges in and

19
00:00:56,289 --> 00:00:58,177
presses outward on the wall.

20
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:02,020
The elastic wall stretches, then springs

21
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,401
back. We measure this pressure in

22
00:01:05,401 --> 00:01:06,964
millimetres of mercury.

23
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:12,092
Now watch one heartbeat.

24
00:01:13,331 --> 00:01:15,856
The heart contracts, and a pressure wave

25
00:01:15,856 --> 00:01:17,631
travels along the artery.

26
00:01:18,867 --> 00:01:20,167
The pressure peaks:

27
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:22,079
this is the systolic pressure.

28
00:01:23,299 --> 00:01:25,461
Then the heart rests, and the pressure

29
00:01:25,461 --> 00:01:26,937
falls to its lowest:

30
00:01:26,937 --> 00:01:28,499
the diastolic pressure.

31
00:01:30,223 --> 00:01:32,611
Together, these two values make your

32
00:01:32,611 --> 00:01:33,298
reading.

33
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:39,233
To measure it, an inflatable cuff goes

34
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,683
around the upper arm.

35
00:01:41,881 --> 00:01:44,481
It squeezes the arm, and a monitor shows

36
00:01:44,481 --> 00:01:47,897
two numbers. The top number is the

37
00:01:47,897 --> 00:01:51,160
systolic pressure, here 120.

38
00:01:52,377 --> 00:01:55,015
The bottom number is the diastolic, here

39
00:01:55,015 --> 00:02:00,181
80. We say this reading is 120 over 80.

40
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:06,838
For most adults, 90 over 60 or lower is

41
00:02:06,838 --> 00:02:11,293
low. The ideal range is between 90 over 60

42
00:02:11,293 --> 00:02:17,314
and 120 over 80. Between 120 over 80 and

43
00:02:17,314 --> 00:02:20,452
140 over 90, you're at risk.

44
00:02:21,668 --> 00:02:24,718
And 140 over 90 or higher is high blood

45
00:02:24,718 --> 00:02:26,880
pressure, called hypertension.

46
00:02:28,568 --> 00:02:30,630
It is diagnosed when readings are that

47
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:32,355
high on two different days.

48
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:38,292
Year after year, high pressure strains the

49
00:02:38,292 --> 00:02:40,404
arteries and damages their walls.

50
00:02:41,635 --> 00:02:43,648
In the heart, that can mean a heart

51
00:02:43,648 --> 00:02:47,338
attack. In the brain, a stroke.

52
00:02:48,579 --> 00:02:50,754
In the kidneys, kidney damage.

53
00:02:52,455 --> 00:02:54,430
And a heart forced to pump harder can

54
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:57,230
eventually fail: that is heart failure.

55
00:03:00,567 --> 00:03:03,117
The good news: you can keep it healthy.

56
00:03:04,327 --> 00:03:07,315
Eat less than 5 grams of salt a day, just

57
00:03:07,315 --> 00:03:08,552
under a teaspoon.

58
00:03:09,791 --> 00:03:11,866
Eat more vegetables and fruit.

59
00:03:13,119 --> 00:03:14,794
Be physically active.

60
00:03:16,063 --> 00:03:18,876
Avoid tobacco, and limit alcohol.

61
00:03:20,611 --> 00:03:22,311
And have your blood pressure checked

62
00:03:22,311 --> 00:03:23,136
regularly.

63
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,688
The most common mistake is thinking:

64
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,437
I feel fine, so my blood pressure must be

65
00:03:31,437 --> 00:03:34,869
normal. But most people with it feel

66
00:03:34,869 --> 00:03:38,378
nothing at all. Only a measurement can

67
00:03:38,378 --> 00:03:42,978
tell. So measure it, and remember:

68
00:03:42,991 --> 00:03:45,291
a diagnosis needs high readings on two

69
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:46,366
different days.

70
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,100
Time for a quick check.

71
00:03:52,332 --> 00:03:56,394
A patient's blood pressure is 150 over 95,

72
00:03:56,394 --> 00:03:57,757
on two different days.

73
00:03:58,996 --> 00:04:00,684
What does that suggest?

74
00:04:01,892 --> 00:04:04,130
Pause the video, and think it through.

75
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:14,079
It suggests high blood pressure, or

76
00:04:14,079 --> 00:04:19,520
hypertension. The systolic value, 150, is

77
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:25,395
above 140. The diastolic value, 95, is

78
00:04:25,395 --> 00:04:29,217
above 90. And it was confirmed on two

79
00:04:29,217 --> 00:04:30,292
different days.

80
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:37,200
Let's recap! Blood pressure is two

81
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,900
numbers, systolic over diastolic.

82
00:04:41,105 --> 00:04:44,617
A reading of 140 over 90 or higher is high

83
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:48,121
blood pressure. And because it is usually

84
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,908
silent, measure it.

85
00:04:51,669 --> 00:04:52,957
Know your numbers.

